(4336081, 622886, 68035, '<td valign="top">I just love this photograph and cant beleive it did not finish higher<br/> <br/>To see the plaza illuminated like this is breathtaking and the fact that the horsemen of the statue are in the dark but that their silhouette is so clear is a fantastic touch (although from other comments that you got I can see that maybe others saw it differently)<br/> <br/>I like the way you burnt the skyline as well to give a real inpenetrable blackness to it<br/> <br/>Beautiful</td>', 'I just love this photograph and cant beleive it did not finish higher To see the plaza illuminated like this is breathtaking and the fact that the horsemen of the statue are in the dark but that their silhouette is so clear is a fantastic touch (although from other comments that you got I can see that maybe others saw it differently) I like the way you burnt the skyline as well to give a real inpenetrable blackness to it Beautiful', '2007-12-26 12:07:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(4336090, 623376, 68035, '<td valign="top">A great ''silky water'' shot that I have no doubt would have done even better but for the fact that there seemed to be a plethora of them in the challenge (says the man who took one of about 1,000,000 moving car lights in the same challenge).  perhaps one of the problems with DPC is that on occasion you can see so many things of beauty that you become a tad blase about them and not appreciate them individually for the wonderous images that they are<br/> <br/>I love the sharpness of the rocks in the foreground and the shells on the beach are another great touch<br/> <br/>Lovely image which like several in the challenge was sadly underrated</td>', 'A great ''silky water'' shot that I have no doubt would have done even better but for the fact that there seemed to be a plethora of them in the challenge (says the man who took one of about 1,000,000 moving car lights in the same challenge).  perhaps one of the problems with DPC is that on occasion you can see so many things of beauty that you become a tad blase about them and not appreciate them individually for the wonderous images that they are I love the sharpness of the rocks in the foreground and the shells on the beach are another great touch Lovely image which like several in the challenge was sadly underrated', '2007-12-26 12:15:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(4336117, 623194, 1024, '<td valign="top">I have been to Europe many times and have to admit that I think traffic circles (American for roundabout) are a truly wonderful invention,  It seems we are beginning to add them to shopping centers and places with light traffic.  I hope they catch on.<br/> <br/>This photo is well done, the streaks of light adding to the eerie night feeling.  I love the twinkles of the street lights.</td>', 'I have been to Europe many times and have to admit that I think traffic circles (American for roundabout) are a truly wonderful invention,  It seems we are beginning to add them to shopping centers and places with light traffic.  I hope they catch on. This photo is well done, the streaks of light adding to the eerie night feeling.  I love the twinkles of the street lights.', '2007-12-26 12:30:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(4336130, 623194, 67152, '<td valign="top">Jon<br/>I liked this a lot - i love roundabouts and the lights turning were really cool.  Gave it a 7 during voting.  I just think a cleaner foreground (lose the tree) would have made this come off a bit better.  Chain saws sure can really come in handy for DPC shots..</td>', 'JonI liked this a lot - i love roundabouts and the lights turning were really cool.  Gave it a 7 during voting.  I just think a cleaner foreground (lose the tree) would have made this come off a bit better.  Chain saws sure can really come in handy for DPC shots..', '2007-12-26 12:34:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(4336133, 622417, 51026, '<td valign="top">Thank you all for the comments!  This is the original shot just converted to black and white.  Levels were played with a little bit.  The shot was take right before sunrise.  Hopefully it doesn''t get disqualified because i dont have the original shot with me.  Home from college until Jan. 14th.  <br/> <br/>Thanks again</td>', 'Thank you all for the comments!  This is the original shot just converted to black and white.  Levels were played with a little bit.  The shot was take right before sunrise.  Hopefully it doesn''t get disqualified because i dont have the original shot with me.  Home from college until Jan. 14th.   Thanks again', '2007-12-26 12:34:21.000000', NULL, 0),
